Models and data used at runtime (fetched by the setup scripts, not distributed
in this repository):

  InLegalBERT  (law-ai/InLegalBERT)
    License: MIT
    A BERT-base encoder further pre-trained on ~5.4M Indian court documents,
    by the Department of Computer Science and Technology, IIT Kharagpur.
    Statigate uses it as a frozen sentence encoder; it is not fine-tuned or
    retrained. Exported to ONNX and INT8-quantised locally by
    scripts/export_inlegalbert_onnx.py.
    https://huggingface.co/law-ai/InLegalBERT

  Apache OpenNLP sentence model  (opennlp-en-ud-ewt-sentence-1.3-2.5.4.bin)
    License: Apache-2.0
    Trained on the Universal Dependencies English Web Treebank.
    Bundled in the ingestion module for sentence segmentation.

  Optional local LLM (only when --llm jlama is used): a general instruction
  model of the operator's choosing (e.g. Qwen2.5-Instruct, Apache-2.0). Not
  distributed here; fetched by scripts/download_jlama_model.py.

The Indian statute corpus in grounding/src/main/resources/statutes/ consists of
condensed editorial summaries authored for this project. Indian legislative
text is not subject to copyright (Copyright Act, 1957, s.52(1)(q)); the
summaries should be checked against the authoritative text on indiacode.nic.in.

